WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.250
In this video, you use the VM right-sizing dashboard in SUSE Observability to find virtual machines that are oversized, undersized, or idle.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:22.800
This dashboard compares the vCPUs and memory each VM is allocated with what it uses, and what the difference costs.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:31.420
The Cluster and VM filters scope every panel. Here, it covers all VMs of the harvester-north cluster.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:40.250
The Savings row estimates the monthly saving from right-sizing running VMs and from removing idle and stopped ones.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.870
Scroll down for the numbers behind the savings.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:54.790
The dashboard counts the vCPUs and memory to give back, and the VMs that are undersized, idle, or stopped.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:01:01.250
Days of data shows how long the measurements cover. Less than a week can miss weekly peaks.

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:08.830
Per VM, you see allocated and recommended vCPUs and what to give back, with memory below.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.060
Scroll further down.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:21.240
The evidence panels show the measurements behind each recommendation, such as CPU at the ninety-fifth percentile.

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:32.120
At the bottom, charts plot utilisation per VM over time against amber and red threshold lines.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:41.689
To apply a recommendation, edit the VM's CPU and memory in SUSE Virtualization, then restart the VM.
